 r←normaliseEvents events;e;int;m
 r←⊃,/normaliseEvent¨events

 e←⌽⊃¨r ⍝ Extract individual events (in reverse order)
 :If ∨/int←⍸(10|⎕DR¨e)∊1 3      ⍝ Numeric codes
    m←int[⍸e[int]∊EVENTNUMS]    ⍝ Recognised numeric events
    e[m]←EVENTNAMES[EVENTNUMS⍳e[m]]
    ⍝ Write the names BACK into r. Previously the conversion happened only in
    ⍝ the local e, which is used for de-duplication, so r kept the numbers --
    ⍝ and fixSendEvents deletes any Event whose codes are still numeric, on the
    ⍝ grounds that numeric events are not sent to the client. The net effect was
    ⍝ that ('Event' 30 'CB'), the canonical ⎕WC registration, silently reached
    ⍝ the client with no Event property at all: menus and mouse handlers were
    ⍝ created and simply never fired. Unrecognised codes are left numeric, which
    ⍝ is what fixSendEvents' filter is actually for.
    r←(⌽e){(⊂⍺),1↓⍵}¨r
 :EndIf
 e←⎕c (2×(2↑¨e)∊⊂'on')↓¨e ⍝ Drop leading 'on'
 r←(⌽(⍳≢e)=e⍳e)/r         ⍝ Pick last

 r←((¯1+≢events)⍴⊂⍬),⊂r   ⍝ Everything merged into last element (in case there were several Event property values)
